-- title:
--   Local index of gΛᵥ in Λᵥ is a power of ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of the project, i.e. $1 \in \Lambda$, $\Lambda$ is closed under multiplication, the $\mathbb{Q}$-span of $\Lambda$ is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and $\Lambda$ is finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-module (maximality is not assumed). Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $\ell$ be a prime number whose image in $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in the prime ideal of $v$, so that $v$ is the place above $\ell$. Write $\Lambda_v$ for [`Submodule.localBox Λ v`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), the additive subgroup of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ generated by the elements $z \otimes c$ with $z \in \Lambda$ and $c$ in the valuation ring of the completion at $v$. Let $g \in \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{Q}_v$ lie in $\Lambda_v$ and be a unit of that ring (no assumption that $g^{-1} \in \Lambda_v$). Then there is a natural number $f$ such that the relative index of the image of $\Lambda_v$ under the additive map $x \mapsto g x$ with respect to $\Lambda_v$ — that is, the index of $g\Lambda_v \cap \Lambda_v$ in $\Lambda_v$, which is the index of $g\Lambda_v$ in $\Lambda_v$ since $g \in \Lambda_v$ forces $g\Lambda_v \subseteq \Lambda_v$ — equals $\ell^{f}$. In particular this index is finite and nonzero.
--
--   This is the local statement that left multiplication by an invertible element of a completed order changes the lattice only by an $\ell$-power index, $\ell$ being the residue characteristic of $v$. It feeds the computation of indices of translated lattices place by place, and is used in [`QuaternionAlgebra.exists_ofFiniteIdele_mul_eq_ofFiniteIdele_mul_mul_iff_relIndex_eq_sq_and_forall_not_le_zsmul`](thm.html#QuaternionAlgebra.exists_ofFiniteIdele_mul_eq_ofFiniteIdele_mul_mul_iff_relIndex_eq_sq_and_forall_not_le_zsmul), where vanishing of the exponent at places away from a given norm identifies the local components that are units of the order.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_QuaternionAlgebra_IsOrder_exists_relIndex_map_mulLeft_localBox_eq_pow.lean

